# qwen36 CUDA tier, the host pool following the card's residents: where Q36CC_FOLLOW_ROWS comes from (2026-10-26)
# An earlier version of this change followed before every prompt chunk of more than 32 rows (Q36CC_STAGE_ROWS)
# once the residents had moved. The same day, on another Google Colab T4 high-RAM VM of the same shape,
# bench.c --session ran origin/dev 77530b49 against it with the conversations of sessions.txt (the same
# commands, a warm-up, then ABBA 4+4); then that version with the diagnostic line below (not part of this change)
# ran each conversation once. Below: the patch, the two reports, the diagnostic's follow and turn lines. In the
# reports below 'v1 pr' is that earlier version, not this change; only bench's reports are kept, not the CSVs of
# their runs.
# What they say, medians of the time to the first token (origin/dev -> that version):
#   chat turn 3, 36 tokens read after a 489-token answer: 0.76 -> 0.90 s; the follow before it moved 317 + 317 experts
#     in 193 ms, so the copies gave back about 53 ms;
#   agent turn 8, 35 tokens after a 467-token answer: 0.93 -> 1.08 s, 239 + 239 moved in 147 ms: about nothing back (-3 ms);
